{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For this commandment.</b> This refers to the Torah, in the manner of (Deuteronomy 8:1) ״כל המצוה אשר אנכי מצוך היום״. <b>It is not too wondrous</b> — its matter is not hidden and concealed so that you cannot do it; and this is what it says, ״לא בשמים היא״ — it is not in the heavens — which is an explanation of ״לא נפלאת היא״; and likewise ״לא מעבר לים״ is an explanation of ״לא רחוקה היא״. And the sea here is the great sea, which is dark, and it is among the things impossible for human beings to be able to enter there because of the darkness of the waters; and the intention is not regarding other seas that human beings can enter, for just as it says ״לא בשמים היא״ and that is a denial, since it is among the things impossible that a person should ascend to the heavens, so too ״מעבר לים״ is a denial."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:24.138164512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}